  "body": "First slice of #361 (vendor STEP tool models): milling.\n\n## What changed\n- **`SetToolBody` (new, undoable: set / replace / clear).** It attaches a holder or assembly mesh (STEP, STL or OBJ, through the existing importer) to a milling tool.\n  - **Placement** is numeric: which model direction is the tool axis, and the model origin's height above the tip.\n  - **Validated at command creation, refusals by name:** non-finite, empty or degenerate meshes; a body whose XY bounds don't contain the axis; a body reaching below the flute top; lathe insert kinds (that is #369).\n  - `ChangeTool`, generation and the post gate also refuse a body that would sit over the flutes.\n- **The revolved envelope** (`crates/tools/src/holder_profile.rs`):\n  - Each triangle is clipped exactly to every band it crosses, and the band takes the farthest clipped vertex. It is exact, so a facet crossing a band with no vertex in it still counts.\n  - Bands are cut at 0.25 mm or more (at most 2048), then merged down to at most 32, each merge keeping the larger radius. The envelope can only grow.\n- **How the checks read it:**\n  - **Fixture collision laws** (upright and posed, `sim/laws.rs`, `posed_steel.rs`, `workholding.rs`) take a `HolderStack` of real bands. `HolderStack::cylinder(geom)` reproduces the old float sums, so a tool without a body is bit-identical.\n  - **Every one-cylinder check** (rest reach, solid law, multi-axis shank dodge, drill reach, cross-drill holder, machine max tool length) sees the tool with its holder replaced by the cylinder enclosing the body (`HolderProfile::enclose`). It is swapped in at three world reads: `collect_job`, the post gate's fixture walk, and the machine check. It can only over-report.\n- **The body is part of the operation stamp** (it can change the generated path). It adds bytes only when present, so existing stamps are unchanged.\n- **Project file v54.** An optional `body` key on the tool row holds the placed facets and placement. The envelope is re-derived on load, never saved, and a bad body refuses the file by name. The bump stops a v53 build from silently dropping the body and judging the smaller cylinder.\n  - **Conflict note:** #354 also takes v54. Whichever merges second renumbers to v55, one line in the ladder plus the `51..=54` rung in `apply.rs`.\n- **Deleting the tool** (`DeleteTool` / `DeleteEntity`) frees the body, and undo restores it.\n- `docs/decisions/368-tool-body-step.md`\n\n## How tested\n- New `holder_profile` unit tests (7), including a facet crossing a band with no vertex in it, and a randomized check that no point on any facet lies outside its band.\n- New `crates/app/tests/tool_body.rs` (8):\n  - A 40 mm collar turns a move the 22 mm cylinder passed into a named holder collision, in generation and in the post gate.\n  - A stepped body (narrow nose, wide flange) passes a post beside the nose that the enclosing cylinder would have hit.\n  - With no body, the stamp and toolpath are identical to before.\n  - Undo/redo walk set, replace and clear.\n  - Save → load → save is byte-identical.\n  - Deleting the tool frees the body, and degenerate input refuses by name.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick upstream/main` (macOS), after merging upstream/main: tools, sim and app suites all green. That includes every existing golden_cl, fixtures, posting, project_roundtrip, commands_undo and drill suite, unchanged.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --tests` is clean, and `cargo check -p camcraft-ui` passes.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No UI: attaching a body is reachable from the command and the project file only. The picking UI and display are #371; ISO 13399 auto-alignment is #370 (stacking on this branch).\n- Not yet in the tool library file (#348).\n\nChangelog: Tools can carry a modelled holder body (STEP/STL/OBJ) placed by axis and tip offset; collision checks judge its revolved envelope (#368)\n\nFixes #368\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
